---
/**
 * Icon — the one icon primitive in the design system.
 *
 * Lucide is the only icon source. Its 24x24 coordinate system, simple line
 * construction and restrained joins match the engineering-notebook direction
 * without introducing a second visual personality. The official path data is
 * vendored below (lucide-static v1.34.0, ISC) rather than installed: no npm
 * dependency, no client JavaScript, no icon font.
 *
 * Every icon inherits `currentColor` and is decorative by default. If an icon
 * is the only visible content of a control, the control itself must carry the
 * `aria-label` — the SVG is never focusable and never the accessible name.
 *
 * Lucide ships no brand glyphs, so GitHub, LinkedIn and ORCID use their
 * official marks (Simple Icons, CC0), rendered as fills. Brand marks are the
 * one sanctioned exception to the stroke system — never redrawn, never
 * approximated, and used only beside their own service's link.
 *
 * Sizes come from --icon-xs (14px), --icon-sm (16px) and --icon-md (18px). The
 * restraint map lives in docs/DESIGN.md: no icons on page navigation, the brand
 * name, headings, eyebrows, badges, timeline entries, publication metadata or
 * prose. Research diagrams may sit a mark beside a mechanism label.
 *
 * Additional glyphs for those diagrams are vendored from lucide-static 0.469.0
 * (ISC), same licence, same 24×24 stroke contract. Do not hand-draw substitutes.
 */
/* Official Lucide path data — do not hand-edit or redraw. The icon name type is
   derived from this object, so the two can never drift apart. */
const PATHS = {
